{
  "id": 307939149,
  "iid": 15956,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "CMake: clear stale PCRE2 cache entry if needed",
  "description": "Prevents build failures on macOS with Homebrew when an old build\ndirectory references an older version of the PCRE2 library.\n\nFixes: v3.7.0rc0-381-gb9f2e4b7fa (\"Make PCRE2 a required dependency\")\n___\nFixes the following situation:\n```\n$ cmake .\n...\n$ time ninja\nninja: error: '/usr/local/Cellar/pcre2/10.42/lib/libpcre2-8.dylib', needed by 'run/libwsutil.0.0.0.dylib', missing and no known rule to make it\n```\nWith the fix:\n```\n$ cmake .\n...\n-- Package PCRE2 has changed, clearing cache.\n-- Found PCRE2: /Library/Developer/CommandLineTools/SDKs/MacOSX13.3.sdk/usr/lib/libpcre2-8.tbd (found version \"10.42\")\n...\n$ ninja\n<succeeds>\n```\nInterestingly it appears to ignore the Homebrew version, but I don't mind as there is some working version:\n```\n$ pkg-config --libs libpcre2-8\n-L/usr/local/Cellar/pcre2/10.43/lib -lpcre2-8\n```",
  "state": "merged",
